---
import LearnLayout from "../../components/LearnLayout.astro";
---

<LearnLayout
  title="Backup: a One-Time License — Learn — cntxt"
  description="The planned one-time-purchase backup, separate from the subscription sync feature."
  path="/learn/backup"
>
  <a href="/learn" class="back-link">← Learn</a>
  <h1>Backup: a one-time license to your own storage</h1>
  <p>
    🔴 Planned — not built yet, no date set.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/learn/sync">Sync</a> keeps your workspaces live across devices,
    which costs us something continuously for as long as you use it — that's
    why it's a subscription. Backup is meant to be the opposite: a single
    purchase that lets you back everything up to a storage provider you
    control, with no ongoing cost on our side and so no ongoing charge on
    yours.
  </p>
  <p>
    The storage provider itself is still being decided. The shape we're
    designing toward: you connect your own account (think your own Google
    Drive or similar), cntxt writes a backup there, and you can restore from
    it on any profile — a safety net you own, not a service we keep running
    for you.
  </p>

  <h2>Status</h2>
  <table class="status-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Capability</th><th>Status</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>One-time-purchase backup to a storage provider you control</td>
        <td>🔴 Planned</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</LearnLayout>
